/-
  E8TrialityCertIV.lean — the negative theorem: no sigma-invariant sqrt2*E8.

  THEOREM (informal). Lambda24 contains no sigma-invariant primitive
  sqrt2*E8 sublattice; equivalently the centralizer of sigma in Co0
  contains no EE8-involution, hence no order-6 isometry g has g^4 = sigma
  and 2A/EE8-type g^3.

  Certified here:
  * f=0 case: `no_index9_saturation` — for EVERY compatible 4-clique of
    omega-hexagons in Q = A2 (x) E8 (all 122850 of them, enumerated inside
    the proof), the 8x16 span matrix has FULL rank mod 3, so the
    saturation index has trivial 3-part and can never be the required 9.
    (Hexagon planes are omega-irreducible — `XQ_no_fixed_vectors` — so a
    primitive omega-invariant sqrt2*E8 would be the index-9 saturation of
    one of its full-rank 4-cliques.)
  * f=2,4,6 cases: for each Carter class A2^k (k=1,2,3) an explicit
    order-3 isometry Ak of E8 with fixed space of exact rank 8-2k
    (rank sandwich: Fk*(Ak-1)=0 plus 2k independent image rows, stacked
    invertible via adjugate certificate) containing an explicit NORM-2
    root rk — but the fixed part of a sigma-invariant sqrt2*E8 must lie
    in R = sqrt3*E8, forcing minimum norm >= 6·(scale) : contradiction.

  Bridges (classical, stated not proven): Carter's classification of
  order-3 Weyl classes as A2^k; the 120 hexagons exhaust the 720 minimal
  vectors of Q (Python-enumerated); Fix(sigma) ≅ sqrt3*E8 is a class
  invariant (certified in E8TrialityCertII).
-/
